            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, qUESTION (Justice Ginsburg): Suppose you have a case in which 10 jurors are excused because of their expressed views on the death penalty, excused by the State. Five of those jurors are white and five are black. But with the five black jurors, the questioning was qualitatively and quantitatively different. It went on much longer with much more searching, a different script. What result then?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "b0ba4bd7ea48eb193b13cfc0f739b5141cc00d9a86f54bb30437442a8beaad96",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-b0ba4bd7ea48-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice (unspecified), qUESTION (Unnamed Justice): Because of the answers that they gave on the questionnaire and \u2014 and answers that they gave just before the script was used."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Oral Argument",
